** vdd<->vss). It now uses XDUT vss vdd vinn vinp vout with canonical node names, exactly like the
** *_biaswrap_ibias sibling. For the AnalogGym DUTs this is a no-op: their vss port binds to
** node `vss`, which `Vss vss 0 dc 0` ties to ground just as the old direct-to-0 wiring did.
.lib tsmc_n65_models.scs tt
.temp 27

.param VDD=1.8
.param VCM=300m
.param CL=10p

Vdd  vdd 0 dc {VDD}
Vss  vss 0 dc 0
Vcm  vinp 0 dc {VCM}          ; common-mode bias on the non-inverting input
Vac  sigin 0 dc 0 ac 1        ; noise input source (input-referral reference)
Lfb  vout vinn 1T        ; 1 TH: DC short (bias), AC open
Cin  vinn sigin 1T        ; 1 TF: DC open, AC inject into the inverting node
CLoad vout 0 {CL}

XDUT vss vdd vinn vinp vout amp_008_leung_nmcf
.control
  set filetype=ascii
  noise v(vout) Vac dec 50 1 1MEG
  print inoise_total onoise_total
  write
  quit
.endc
